        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): surface diagnostic warning when inline keyboard buttons silently dropped due to 64-byte callback_data limit",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\n`sanitizeTelegramCallbackData` silently drops inline keyboard buttons whose `callback_data` exceeds Telegram's 64-byte limit. When all buttons are dropped, `buildInlineKeyboard` returns `undefined`, and the message is delivered as text-only with `ok: true` — making the keyboard loss completely undetectable.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nWithout a diagnostic signal, operators have no way to know interactive keyboard buttons were silently stripped. This adds `diagLogger.warn` at both `sendMessageTelegramWithContext` and `sendLocationTelegramWithContext` to surface the loss.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nOperators now see a diagnostic warning when inline keyboard buttons are dropped due to Telegram's 64-byte `callback_data` limit. Message delivery behavior is unchanged — messages still go through as text-only — but the issue is now visible.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- 24/24 tests pass in `extensions/telegram/src/approval-callback-data.test.ts`\r\n- Fixed a test byte-count mismatch: `\"€\".repeat(21) + \"x\"` (64 bytes) → `\"€\".repeat(21) + \"xx\"` (65 bytes), matching the label \"multi-byte utf8 overflow at 65 bytes\"\r\n- -`button-types.live-proof.test.ts` exercises the real `createSubsystemLogger` (no mock)  and captures `console.warn` output, confirming the diagnostic fires for both  `buildTelegramPresentationButtons` and `buildTelegramInteractiveButtons`:\r\n[telegram] inline keyboard: 1 of 2 button(s) dropped — callback_data likely exceeds Telegram 64-byte limit. \r\n[telegram] inline keyboard: 1 of 1 button(s) dropped — callback_data likely exceeds Telegram 64-byte limit. Message delivered as text-only. \r\n[telegram] inline keyboard: 1 of 2 button(s) dropped — callback_data likely exceeds Telegram 64-byte limit.\r\n\r\n| File | Change |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `extensions/telegram/src/send.ts` | +10 lines — diagnostic warnings in 2 send paths |\r\n| `extensions/telegram/src/approval-callback-data.test.ts` | +17/-0 lines — test boundary case fix |\r\n\r\nRelated to #106996",
        "branch": "fix/tg-keyboard-callback-drop-106996",
